# ERP project principles

This repository is a TypeScript monorepo.

Applications:

- `apps/api` is the Node.js backend (`@erp/api`)
- `apps/web` is the Next.js frontend (`@erp/web`)

Shared packages:

- `@erp/contracts` holds Zod schemas and API transport contracts
- `@erp/ui` holds reusable UI primitives, layout, patterns, and the future ERP theme
- `@erp/typescript-config` holds shared TypeScript configuration
- `@erp/eslint-config` holds shared lint configuration
- `@erp/test-utils` holds shared test helpers

General engineering rules:

- TypeScript strict mode is mandatory.
- Never introduce `any` without explicit justification.
- Prefer `unknown` at external boundaries and validate before use.
- Organize code primarily by business feature.
- Reuse existing abstractions before creating new ones.
- Keep architectural boundaries explicit.
- Never weaken lint or TypeScript rules merely to make code compile.
- Run lint, typecheck, architecture checks, and relevant tests after implementation.
- Do not duplicate API contracts between frontend and backend.
- External input must always be validated.
- Material UI is the only primary UI framework. Do not add Tailwind, shadcn/ui, or another styling system.
- Do not create generic `helpers`, `misc`, `common`, or `utils` folders unless the code has one cohesive purpose.
- Import shared packages through their public package exports. Do not deep-import package internals.
